# Famouskai syntax sample: log files (plugins/ace-custom/mode-log.js)
# One release day of a small local-first web app, seen through six kinds of logs.
# Lines that start with # or = are comments. Fold arrows appear on stack traces
# (an Error line followed by "at" lines) and on every Famous Mark header below.
# All names, addresses and paths are examples: no real user, host or account.

# ﹥ 1. Local web server (access log, Common Log Format)
# Offline mode needs HTTPS or localhost, so the app is served locally for testing:
# python3 -m http.server 8080 --bind 127.0.0.1
127.0.0.1 - - [25/Oct/2026:09:00:01 +0900] "GET / HTTP/1.1" 200 -
127.0.0.1 - - [25/Oct/2026:09:00:01 +0900] "GET /style.css HTTP/1.1" 200 -
127.0.0.1 - - [25/Oct/2026:09:00:01 +0900] "GET /plugins/ext-famous-core.js HTTP/1.1" 200 -
127.0.0.1 - - [25/Oct/2026:09:00:02 +0900] "GET /sw.js HTTP/1.1" 200 -
127.0.0.1 - - [25/Oct/2026:09:00:02 +0900] "GET /manifest.json HTTP/1.1" 200 -
127.0.0.1 - - [25/Oct/2026:09:00:03 +0900] "GET /favicon.ico HTTP/1.1" 404 -
192.168.1.20 - - [25/Oct/2026:09:04:12 +0900] "GET /index.html HTTP/1.1" 200 -
# A phone on the same network gets the page, but no offline mode: plain http on a LAN address.

